INDEPENDENT DERIVATION — S11c-a §3c shifted-trace law
Truncation: first order in epsilon (wave), first order in eta (shape).

========================================================================
CASE: (a) background identically zero  [f0=0, dw_f0=0]
------------------------------------------------------------------------
W_bg               = W0*(eta*w1 + 1)
h_s0 = s*W_bg/2    = W0*eta*s*w1/2 + W0*s/2
h_s  = h_s0+eps*dh = W0*eta*s*w1/2 + W0*s/2 + delta_h*epsilon
w_flat = s*W0/2    = W0*s/2
f0_flat            = 0
dw_f0_flat         = 0
df_flat            = df_at_flat
dw_df_flat         = dw_df_at_flat

COMPOSITION delta[f(x,h_s)]  (O(eps^1), O(eta^0..1)):
  W0*dw_df_at_flat*eta*s*w1/2 + df_at_flat

SECTION 3c LAW  df(x,h_s0) + dh*dw_f0(x,h_s0)  (O(eta^0..1)):
  W0*dw_df_at_flat*eta*s*w1/2 + df_at_flat

RESIDUAL (composition - law): 0

FROZEN-AT-FLAT (wrong) df(flat)+dh*dw_f0(flat):
  df_at_flat
RESIDUAL (composition - frozen): W0*dw_df_at_flat*eta*s*w1/2

TERM CENSUS (each monomial and whether it carries eta):
  term=df_at_flat   has_eta=False
  term=W0*dw_df_at_flat*eta*s*w1/2   has_eta=True

========================================================================
CASE: (b) background nonzero WITH nonzero normal derivative
------------------------------------------------------------------------
W_bg               = W0*(eta*w1 + 1)
h_s0 = s*W_bg/2    = W0*eta*s*w1/2 + W0*s/2
h_s  = h_s0+eps*dh = W0*eta*s*w1/2 + W0*s/2 + delta_h*epsilon
w_flat = s*W0/2    = W0*s/2
f0_flat            = f0_at_flat
dw_f0_flat         = dw_f0_at_flat
df_flat            = df_at_flat
dw_df_flat         = dw_df_at_flat

COMPOSITION delta[f(x,h_s)]  (O(eps^1), O(eta^0..1)):
  W0*dw_df_at_flat*eta*s*w1/2 + delta_h*dw_f0_at_flat + df_at_flat

SECTION 3c LAW  df(x,h_s0) + dh*dw_f0(x,h_s0)  (O(eta^0..1)):
  W0*dw_df_at_flat*eta*s*w1/2 + delta_h*dw_f0_at_flat + df_at_flat

RESIDUAL (composition - law): 0

FROZEN-AT-FLAT (wrong) df(flat)+dh*dw_f0(flat):
  delta_h*dw_f0_at_flat + df_at_flat
RESIDUAL (composition - frozen): W0*dw_df_at_flat*eta*s*w1/2

TERM CENSUS (each monomial and whether it carries eta):
  term=df_at_flat   has_eta=False
  term=delta_h*dw_f0_at_flat   has_eta=False
  term=W0*dw_df_at_flat*eta*s*w1/2   has_eta=True

========================================================================
CASE: (c) density-like: nonzero bg, w-independent  [dw_f0=0]  (supplied §3c density)
------------------------------------------------------------------------
W_bg               = W0*(eta*w1 + 1)
h_s0 = s*W_bg/2    = W0*eta*s*w1/2 + W0*s/2
h_s  = h_s0+eps*dh = W0*eta*s*w1/2 + W0*s/2 + delta_h*epsilon
w_flat = s*W0/2    = W0*s/2
f0_flat            = f0_at_flat
dw_f0_flat         = 0
df_flat            = df_at_flat
dw_df_flat         = dw_df_at_flat

COMPOSITION delta[f(x,h_s)]  (O(eps^1), O(eta^0..1)):
  W0*dw_df_at_flat*eta*s*w1/2 + df_at_flat

SECTION 3c LAW  df(x,h_s0) + dh*dw_f0(x,h_s0)  (O(eta^0..1)):
  W0*dw_df_at_flat*eta*s*w1/2 + df_at_flat

RESIDUAL (composition - law): 0

FROZEN-AT-FLAT (wrong) df(flat)+dh*dw_f0(flat):
  df_at_flat
RESIDUAL (composition - frozen): W0*dw_df_at_flat*eta*s*w1/2

TERM CENSUS (each monomial and whether it carries eta):
  term=df_at_flat   has_eta=False
  term=W0*dw_df_at_flat*eta*s*w1/2   has_eta=True

========================================================================
SUMMARY — what the law requires for physical fields in this scope
========================================================================

From composition:
  delta[f(x,h_s)] = df(x, h_s0) + dh * dw_f0(x, h_s0)
  with h_s0 = s*W_bg/2 = s*W0/2 + eta*(s*W0*w1/2)

Expanding df(x,h_s0) about the flat face to O(eta):
  df(x,h_s0) = df(flat) + eta*(s*W0*w1/2)*dw_df(flat) + O(eta^2)

So two structural pieces, distinct in role:
  (1) PERTURBATION EVALUATION FACE: df is evaluated at h_s0 (carries eta through W_bg),
      NOT frozen at w = s*W0/2. The eta*dw_df piece is O(eps)*O(eta) and is retained
      at first shape order (§2a: do not drop mixed bookkeepers).
  (2) BACKGROUND NORMAL JET: dh * dw_f0(x,h_s0). This is present only when the
      supplied background has nonzero dw_f0. Per §3c / §2d in this scope:
        v_bulk^0 = 0,  delta_p^0 = 0,  j^0 = 0  =>  dw_f0 = 0 for those
        rho_4D,bg^0 depends on in-plane anchor, not on w  =>  dw_rho0 = 0
      Therefore NO free premise jet may be invented; the jet term vanishes because
      the supplied background makes it vanish, not because the law was truncated.

Conormal on an ARBITRARY probe field is not one of the supplied physical fields:
its shifted-evaluation term (the eta*dw_df piece for a generic probe) must be left
intact — it is an operator identity, not a physical-field specialisation.

case (a) residual composition-vs-law: 0
case (b) residual composition-vs-law: 0
case (c) residual composition-vs-law: 0
